.TH htget 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
htget \- fetch a page over HTTP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B htget
.I url
.I file
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B htget
fetches
.I url
and writes the body to
.IR file .
It understands chunked replies, so what lands in the file is the page
and not the HTTP framing.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# htget http://example.com/ page.htm
# htget http://127.0.0.1:8080/index.html got.htm
.fi
.SH NOTES
HTTP only.  For HTTPS use
.BR tlsget (1),
which takes the address and the name separately.
.PP
The radio must be up and
.B /etc/resolv.conf
written; see
.BR wifi (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tlsget (1),
.BR httpd (1),
.BR wifi (1),
.BR dig (1)
